You are debugging a production issue where a high-throughput payment settlement service is intermittently losing audit records and executing database writes synchronously despite being marked for asynchronous background execution. The lead developer wrote the following Spring bean:

java
@Service
public class SettlementService {
    @Autowired
    private TransactionRepository repository;

    public void processSettlementBatch(List<SettlementRecord> batch) {
        for (SettlementRecord record : batch) {
            executeSettlement(record);
        }
    }

    @Async
    @Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRES_NEW)
    public void executeSettlement(SettlementRecord record) {
        record.setProcessedTimestamp(System.currentTimeMillis());
        repository.save(record);
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where an ultra-low-latency routing service running on a multi-core ARM64 server exhibits intermittent `NullPointerException`s and reads partially initialized fields of `RouteConfig`. The following Double-Checked Locking singleton pattern was implemented:

java
public class RouteManager {
    private static RouteConfig instance;

    public static RouteConfig getInstance(String profile) {
        if (instance == null) {
            synchronized (RouteManager.class) {
                if (instance == null) {
                    instance = new RouteConfig(profile);
                }
            }
        }
        return instance;
    }
}
